{"kind":"report","text":"Approved LV4 at 9f21246141ebee613165dd93696068328e71afb6, tree b23966991c32fc83a538ece8940d3192934a5f32. The passing gate tested clean head 957db0f1e35529e071477484830f7d39ff7671ee, tree d5fa74b947693ffb3b7dabf1cbae33d22f6a5066. The final commit adds only the evidence note. I matched all 25 cited hashes, including the earlier failed gate, and independently ran 46 client, CLI, and MCP tests. The committed room asset matches the reproduced digest.\n\nArchitecture. The CLI selects the pinned live level, reads its generation and revisions, and uses the live action route. Live replies carry generation and tick. The installed projection binds the result to the query and uses the same ownership path as recorded projections. The retained Native witness exercises enter, renew, leave, and a reset with unchanged journal and storage.\n\nSecurity. The mounted tool checks its cut, installed scope, current generation, and subject revision before signing. Native act ingress checks the read session and exact scope and genesis. The last remote binding proof precedes the synchronous local judgment and commit. The witness changes the installation observed by that proof and checks refusal with unchanged live state in that case. The earlier local tick is returned for an accepted retry after its binding is rechecked. A remote change after the final proof remains outside the ordering guarantee in ruling 8163372d.\n\nSimplification. The live tool reuses the bounded projection and declared card path. Live outcomes stay in the mounted view's result cache. They produce no recorded receipt or custody row. The corrected client tests keep the existing package dependency boundary.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f00d03a205b02231cd1c20d543f123c559abbc37","binding":"assigned","head":"9f21246141ebee613165dd93696068328e71afb6","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fb1c71f752094503